## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/blend.html
- Summary (EN): Combines two inputs, which can be layers, VDBs or attributes, into one result. By default it replaces the background with the foreground, and a mask can fade between the two images.
- Résumé (FR) : Compose un premier plan sur un arrière-plan selon un mode de fusion, avec un masque optionnel pour un fondu entre les deux images.

- Inputs meaning: ["bg: background that the foreground is blended onto", "fg: foreground, the top or source layer in the blend", "mask (optional): per-pixel mask scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by the source", "Space: Image, Texture, Pixel or World, controlling how foreground and background pixels are matched", "Border: defaults to the layer's own border property", "Filter: sampling method", "Mask: how much of the new value is mixed in (default 1, only the new value); also selects the RGBA channels affected", "Toggle RGB, Red, Green, Blue, Alpha: channels the node affects", "Mode: compositing operation such as Blend, Over, Add, Multiply, Screen, Difference, Overlay, Hue or Color", "Alpha Compositing: applies alpha rules to RGBA layers; monochrome layers are treated as opaque", "Swap FG and BG: matters only for non-commutative operators", "Compare Lengths: for Maximum and Minimum modes, picks the output by vector length", "Clip by Data Window and Crop to Content"]

- Caveats: ["With Border Auto and a Constant border property on the input, the Clip border behavior is used", "RGBA inputs are assumed to be premultiplied for blending and alpha compositing", "Clip by Data Window produces a hard edge", "Swap FG and BG has no effect with commutative operators", "To blend normal maps, use the Combine Normals COP instead"]

